Chlorine, with seven valence electrons, acquires that electron. As a result,
a chlorine atom becomes a stable Cl− anion.

The force of attraction between the 1+ charge on the sodium cation
and the 1− charge on the chloride anion creates the ionic bond in sodium
chloride. Recall that sodium chloride is the scientific name for table salt.
