When we read the names of these ions out loud, we say “copper one ion”
or “copper two ion.”

The name of a simple anion is also formed from the name of the
element, but it ends in -ide. Thus, Cl− is the chloride ion, O2− is the oxide
ion, and P3− is the phosphide ion.

The Names of Ions Are Used to Name an Ionic Compound
Naming binary ionic compounds is simple.The name is made up of just two
words: the name of the cation followed by the name of the anion.

