rhodium in these converters act as catalysts and increase the rate of the
decomposition of NO and of NO2 into N2 and O2, harmless gases already
found in the atmosphere. Catalytic converters also speed the change of
CO into CO2 and the change of unburned hydrocarbons into CO2 and
H2O. These hydrocarbons are involved in the formation of ozone and
smog, so it is important that unburned fuel does not come out in the
exhaust.

