for the solid at −78.5°C. Therefore, solid carbon dioxide sublimes at this
temperature. This sublimation point is equivalent to the normal boiling
point of a liquid such as water. Because dry ice is at equilibrium with
carbon dioxide gas at −78.5°C, it is frequently used to provide this low
temperature in the laboratory.

