ward reaction must be greater than the rate of the reverse reaction.
Because the forward reaction is increasing, the equilibrium is said to shift
right. The reactant concentration will continue to drop until the reaction
reaches equilibrium. Then, the forward and reverse reaction rates will be
equal. Remember that changes in the amounts of solids and pure liquids do
